S. Common symbolic layer (A3)
==============================================================================================================
  j = 4 pi G dL_M/dg = a*g/(a + g);  h = (-s**2 + 2*(s + 1)*(s - log(s + 1)))/(s + 1);  h' = s**2/(s + 1)**2
  [PASS] S1 flux j = g a/(g + a) (law S, CT5 S1)
  [PASS] S2 dL_M/d ln a^2 = (a^2/8 pi G) h(g/a)
  [PASS] S3 h' = s^2/(1+s)^2 > 0, h -> s - 2 ln s (tail)

==============================================================================================================
T1. Algebraic (locally responding) tie: response strength, M_L band
==============================================================================================================
  delta ln a^2 = -H*kappa**2*q**2*Derivative(P(q), (q, 2))/(8*pi*(q*Derivative(P(q), q) - P(q)))
  [PASS] T1a delta ln a = -(kappa^2/8 pi)(S_E/2) h: eta = eps S_E/2, S_E = q^2 P''/E (fixed by the tie up to one stiffness)
  [PASS] T1a' P = Z q^2/2 gives S_E = 2, eta = eps (CT5's slaving r[1 + eps h] = 1)
  P = Z q^n/n: S_E = n (E > 0 needs n > 1, so S_E > 1 for every power law)
  dj/dg = (a**2 + a_p*g**2)/(a + g)**2  (a_p = da_loc/dg)
  [PASS] T1b' dj/dg < 0 iff da_loc/dg < -(a_loc/g)^2 (any response law)
  leading-order pole: 1/(1+s)^2 = eta h'(s) -> s* = [1/sqrt(eta)]
  sigma=+1 eta 9.947e-03: pole x* =    10.142  x* sqrt(eta) = 1.0115  band to x 1.004e+02  inside G1 range: canonical True, alt True
  sigma=+1 eta 1.000e-03: pole x* =    31.688  x* sqrt(eta) = 1.0021  band to x 9.990e+02  inside G1 range: canonical True, alt True
  sigma=+1 eta 1.000e-04: pole x* =   100.031  x* sqrt(eta) = 1.0003  band to x 9.990e+03  inside G1 range: canonical True, alt False
  sigma=+1 eta 1.000e-05: pole x* =   316.241  x* sqrt(eta) = 1.0000  band to x 9.990e+04  inside G1 range: canonical False, alt False
  sigma=+1 eta 1.000e-06: pole x* =  1000.005  x* sqrt(eta) = 1.0000  band to x 9.990e+05  inside G1 range: canonical False, alt False
  [PASS] T1b reproduces CT5's pole x = 10.14 at eta = eps
         (x* = 10.1418)
  [PASS] T1b band exists for every eta tested and x* sqrt(eta) -> 1 (x* = eta^-1/2 (1 + O(eta^1/2)))
  band onset inside the G1 range iff eta >= 8.60e-05 (canonical) / 1.25e-04 (alt), i.e. S_E >= 0.017 / 0.025 at kappa 1/2
  [PASS] T1c sigma = -1 (a rises): dj/dg > 0 on x in [1e-3, 1e6] for eta in {eps, 1e-3, 0.1}: NO M_L band (counterexample to T1 as posed)
         (min dj/dg = 1.581e-05)
  T1d: an algebraic variable has no kinetic term; on FRW (h = 0) its equation P'(q) = Pi (or P'(chi) = 0) fixes q: w = -1 exactly.
  [PASS] T1d algebraic FRW equation has no time derivative: q constant, rho constant, w = -1

