T2. Locally inert scalar P(X, phi): exact tie, kinetic energy, gradient sign
==============================================================================================================
  rho_X = P_X + 2 X P_XX = 0  ->  Eq(P(X), C1 + C2*sqrt(X))
  [PASS] T2a rho independent of X iff P = C1 + C2 sqrt(X) (cuscuton): the only X-free exact tie
  cuscuton P = mu^2 sqrt(2X) - V: rho = V(phi), rho + p = sqrt(2)*sqrt(X)*mu**2 (w != -1, cannot cross)
  [covariant rho(X, phi)] K_s = (-kappa**2*s**2/8 + kappa**2*(s + 1)*(s - log(s + 1))/4 + pi*(s + 1))/(pi*(s + 1))
  K_t = (-6*kappa**2*s**2*v**2 + 3*kappa**2*s*v**2*(s + 1)**2 + kappa**2*s*(2*V0 + v**2)*(s + 1)**2 + kappa**2*s*(2*V0 - 4*s**2*v**2 + s*(2*V0 + v**2) - 2*v**2) - 2*kappa**2*(2*V0 + v**2)*(s + 1)**2*log(s + 1) + 8*pi*(2*V0 + v**2)*(s + 1)**2)/(8*pi*(2*V0 + v**2)*(s + 1)**2)
  [PASS] T2b K_s = 1 + eps h(s) (canonical)
  [PASS] T2b general P(X): K_s = P_X + eps h rho_X (no flip when P_X > 0 and rho_X > 0)
         (residual 0)
  K_t(s, 1+w) = (-3*kappa**2*opw*s*(2*s - (s + 1)**2) + 2*kappa**2*s*(s + 1)**2 - kappa**2*s*(opw*(4*s**2 + 3) - 2*s - 2) - 4*kappa**2*(s + 1)**2*log(s + 1) + 16*pi*(s + 1)**2)/(16*pi*(s + 1)**2)
  1+w = 0.0001: min K_t +1.0000e+00  min K_s +1.0000e+00  max c_s^2 = K_s/K_t 1.0001
  1+w = 0.0500: min K_t +1.0000e+00  min K_s +1.0000e+00  max c_s^2 = K_s/K_t 1.0256
  1+w = 0.1000: min K_t +1.0000e+00  min K_s +1.0000e+00  max c_s^2 = K_s/K_t 1.0526
  1+w = 0.3000: min K_t +1.0000e+00  min K_s +1.0000e+00  max c_s^2 = K_s/K_t 1.1765
  1+w = 1.0000: min K_t +9.9989e-01  min K_s +1.0000e+00  max c_s^2 = K_s/K_t 2.0000
  1+w = 1.9000: min K_t +9.7388e-01  min K_s +1.0000e+00  max c_s^2 = K_s/K_t 20.0000
